eather."},{"text":"this was a major network decision."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-008","slides":[{"text":"trl had teenagers screaming outside a window in times square"},{"text":"for the privilege of watching a video"},{"text":"get cut off after forty seconds."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-009","slides":[{"text":"vh1 was for people who thought mtv was too loud."},{"text":"it was."},{"text":"that was the point."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-010","slides":[{"text":"the commercials on these tapes are better than the videos."},{"text":"don't tell the bands."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-011","slides":[{"text":"mtv stopped playing music videos"},{"text":"and nobody at the network could explain when."},{"text":"it just kind of happened."},{"text":"like weather."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-012","slides":[{"text":"every vhs tape of mtv has tracking lines."},{"text":"the good ones have tracking lines on top of tracking lines."},{"text":"someone recorded over a recording"},{"text":"because the new videos were better."},{"text":"they were wrong, but the tape doesn't judge."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-013","slides":[{"text":"yo! mtv raps debuted in 1988."},{"text":"fab 5 freddy hosted."},{"text":"for a lot of suburban kids"},{"text":"that show was the entire culture."},{"text":"arriving through a cable box"},{"text":"in the basement."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-014","slides":[{"text":"directors made music videos to get noticed by hollywood."},{"text":"it worked."},{"text":"then they stopped making music videos."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-015","slides":[{"text":"the real world premiered in 1992."},{"text":"seven strangers. one house. no scripts."},{"text":"it cost almost nothing to produce."},{"text":"a music video cost half a million dollars."},{"text":"the math was simple."},{"text":"the music never had a chance."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-016","slides":[{"text":"someone hit record."},{"text":"left the room."},{"text":"came back three hours later."},{"text":"the tape is here."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-017","slides":[{"text":"video killed the radio star."},{"text":"reality tv killed the video star."},{"text":"nobody wrote a song about that."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-018","slides":[{"text":"bet's rap city was the basement."},{"text":"literally. the set was a basement."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-019","slides":[{"text":"record labels spent millions producing music videos."},{"text":"then gave them to mtv for free."},{"text":"mtv aired them between commercials"},{"text":"and charged the advertisers."},{"text":"the labels made the content."},{"text":"the channel made the money."},{"text":"this went on for twenty years before anyone blinked."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-020","slides":[{"text":"the mtv moon man was a flag on the moon."},{"text":"they were not being subtle about their ambitions."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-021","slides":[{"text":"120 minutes aired at midnight on sundays."},{"text":"it played the bands mtv wouldn't touch during the day."},{"text":"the ratings were tiny."},{"text":"the influence was enormous."},{"text":"every band you like from the '90s"},{"text":"got their first tv airplay at midnight on a sunday."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-022","slides":[{"text":"michael jackson's thriller video had a premiere."},{"text":"on television."},{"text":"for a music video."},{"text":"that used to be possible."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-023","slides":[{"text":"the label said make it three minutes."},{"text":"the director said make it seven."},{"text":"mtv played the whole thing."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-024","slides":[{"text":"someone's dad accidentally taped over a wedding"},{"text":"with four hours of vh1 countdowns."},{"text":"the wedding is gone."},{"text":"the countdown survived."},{"text":"we are not here to judge priorities."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-025","slides":[{"text":"mtv had an entire news division."},{"text":"with a desk and everything."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-026","slides":[{"text":"the vcr made every viewer a programmer."},{"text":"hit record at the right time"},{"text":"and you had your own music channel."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-027","slides":[{"text":"there was a brief window"},{"text":"where being a vj was a real job"},{"text":"with benefits and a parking spot."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-028","slides":[{"text":"in 1982, cable operators didn't want to carry mtv."},{"text":"so mtv ran ads telling kids to call their cable company"},{"text":"and say \"i want my mtv.\""},{"text":"mick jagger did one. pete townshend did one."},{"text":"the kids called."},{"text":"the cable operators caved."},{"text":"a music channel bullied its way onto your television"},{"text":"using peer pressure and rock stars."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-029","slides":[{"text":"mtv unplugged was supposed to be a gimmick."},{"text":"strip the production. acoustic guitars. stools."},{"text":"turns out some bands were better without the arena."},{"text":"the unplugged albums outsold the real albums."},{"text":"nobody at the network saw that coming."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-030","slides":[{"text":"a music video cost more than the album it promoted."},{"text":"lasted four minutes."},{"text":"aired once at 3 am on a tuesday."},{"text":"and it made careers."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-031","slides":[{"text":"every generation got mtv at a different moment."},{"text":"every generation thinks their moment was the real one."},{"text":"every generation is correct."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-032","slides":[{"text":"in 1981, mtv played the same thirty videos on a loop."},{"text":"the labels hadn't figured out yet"},{"text":"that they should send more."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-033","slides":[{"text":"the best part of these tapes is the parts between the videos."},{"text":"the station ids. the bumpers. the vj walking back on set."},{"text":"the stuff nobody meant to save."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-034","slides":[{"text":"they called it music television."},{"text":"both words were eventually optional."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]},{"id":"ratv-035","slides":[{"text":"somebody at mtv networks looked at the ratings"},{"text":"and realized more people watched seven strangers argue"},{"text":"than watched the number one video in the country."},{"text":"that was the day."},{"text":"we don't talk about that day."},{"text":"radio-active tv."}]}],"audio":[{"filename":"godspeedsound---19.mp3","title":"19","artist":"Godspeedsound","url":"https://godspeedsound.bandcamp.com/track/--19","license":"by"},{"filename":"godspeedsound---23.mp3","title":"23","artist":"Godspeedsound","url":"https://godspeedsound.bandcamp.com/track/--23","license":"by"},{"filename":"experimentalrecords-midnight-2.mp3","title":"Midnight 2","artist":"Experimentalrecords","url":"https://experimentalrecords.bandcamp.com/track/midnight-2","license":"by"},{"filename":"experimentalrecords-s-e-a-w-a-v-e-s.mp3","title":"S E A W A V E S","artist":"Experimentalrecords","url":"https://experimentalrecords.bandcamp.com/track/s-e-a-w-a-v-e-s","license":"by"},{"filename":"experimentalrecords-someday.mp3","title":"Someday","artist":"Experimentalrecords","url":"https://experimentalrecords.bandcamp.com/track/someday","license":"by"},{"filename":"buddyrecords-out-of-mind.mp3","title":"Out Of Mind","artist":"Buddyrecords","url":"https://buddyrecords.bandcamp.com/track/out-of-mind","license":"by"},{"filename":"buddyrecords-tuli-on-irti.mp3","title":"Tuli On Irti","artist":"Buddyrecords","url":"https://buddyrecords.bandcamp.com/track/tuli-on-irti","license":"by"},{"filename":"buddyrecords-calacetea.mp3"